   "body": "/claim cloud/m4q-reliab-opus\n\nRe-checked on `dev-swift` @ 90b23273: still true. `SwiftHFRApp.swift:104-105` runs `MPNotificationCenter().prepare()` at launch, and that calls `requestAuthorization` even when logged out.\n\nOverlap: #1247 touches `MPNotificationOpenTests.swift` only. No open PR touches `SwiftHFRApp.swift`, `AppLifecycle.swift`, `MPNotificationCenter.swift` or `MultiWindowTests.swift`.\n\nPlan (HIG › Privacy, ask in context):\n- At launch: only register the `mp` category (no prompt).\n- When an account becomes current (restore of a stored account, login, switch: the existing `AppLifecycle.currentAccountChanged`), ask once, and only if iOS never asked (`.notDetermined`) and « Notifications » or « Badge » is on. Logged out: never ask. The existing Réglages path stays.\n- A pure rule with a test, plus `AppLifecycle` tests through its `Steps` seam:\n  - logged out → no request;\n  - account current → one request;\n  - already decided → none.\n  These tests are written first and red today.\n- LOT-140 doc and a Ledger row: this deliberately differs from legacy's launch request (`HFRswift/Swift/HFRswiftApp.swift:27-29` @ `87fe0d1c`).\n- Draft PR with `compile-check`, then a Fable review.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
